# 16. JWT security checklist

When implementing JWT authentication, remember:

### ① Use HTTPS

Never send authentication tokens over plain HTTP.

```text
HTTPS
  ↓
encrypted transport
```

### ② Use short-lived access tokens

Don't make access tokens unnecessarily long-lived.

### ③ Protect signing keys

Your private key/secret must never be committed to Git.

Bad:

```java
String secret = "my-super-secret-key";
```

Better:

```text
environment variable
secret manager
configuration management
```

### ④ Validate claims

Don't only check the signature.

Also validate:

```text
exp
iss
aud
nbf
```

as appropriate for your architecture.

### ⑤ Don't put sensitive data in the payload

Remember:

```text
JWT payload ≠ encrypted storage
```

### ⑥ Protect refresh tokens carefully

A stolen refresh token can be especially powerful.

