# 17. The most important mental model

If you're learning backend development, I would remember JWT like this:

```text
                JWT
                 │
       ┌─────────┴─────────┐
       │                   │
    Structure            Purpose
       │                   │
 Header.Payload       Authentication
 .Signature           Authorization
       │
       ├── Header
       │
       ├── Payload
       │    └── Claims
       │
       └── Signature
            └── Integrity
```

And the complete authentication picture:

```text
User
 │
 │ username + password
 ▼
Authentication Server
 │
 │ authenticate
 ▼
JWT
 │
 │ Authorization: Bearer JWT
 ▼
API Server
 │
 ├── verify signature
 ├── verify expiration
 ├── verify issuer/audience
 ├── identify user
 └── check permissions
        │
        ▼
     Resource
```

## Where JWT fits in your Java backend roadmap

For your current **Java → Spring → Spring Boot** learning path, I'd put it here:

```text
Java fundamentals
      ↓
HTTP / Web fundamentals
      ↓
Servlet / Tomcat concepts
      ↓
Spring Framework
      ↓
Spring Boot
      ↓
REST API
      ↓
HTTP + JSON
      ↓
Spring Security
      ↓
Authentication
      ↓
JWT
      ↓
OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect
      ↓
Production security
```

So I wouldn't start with JWT immediately. **First understand HTTP, REST, authentication, sessions/cookies, and Spring Security; then JWT becomes much easier to understand instead of just memorizing configuration.**
